  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a reader of a long topic, I want to see only the posts quoted at least N times (plus whitelisted authors), so that I catch up on what mattered.\n\n### Scope\n\nWalk topic pages from a start page, keep messages quoted ≥ N times (LOT-032) or written by a whitelisted pseudo (input list), stop after a result batch (legacy: 40) and report where to resume; progress stream; cookie-less page fetches unless the spec proves the legacy used the session (flag side effect, E25).\n\n- Module: HFRClient · Difficulty: medium · Priority: medium · post-MVP\n- Implements: legacy parity (no FEAT)\n- Absorbs: Phase 4 backlog 'filtered-posts use case (C11, candidate for HFRClient)'; 'post filter' in FEATURES 'Not to lose'\n- Legacy sources (read-only, `origin/master`): `FavoritePostFilterService.swift`, `Classes/FilterPostsQuotes.m`, `Classes/ObjCFilteredPostsRendererWorker.m`; legacy backlog HFR-031 ('Résultats suivants')\n- Spec: `docs/lots/LOT-093-*.md`\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-030 (#57, done)\n- LOT-032 (#59, done)\n- LOT-045 (#71, done)\n\n### Blocked by\n\nnone: every dependency is merged (unblocked 2026-10-29, steward ext/opus-helper1)\n\n### Model\n\nSonnet → Opus (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- none known; any page state the spec needs and the fixtures lack is listed as *pending capture*, never hand-built (LESSONS 35-36)\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Same selection as legacy on the LOT-003 topic fixtures (differential test), including quotes of quotes as legacy counts them.\n- [ ] Batch limit and resume page reported; cancellation honoured between pages.\n- [ ] Whether the session is used is decided in the spec from the legacy code, with the flag side effect stated.\n- [ ] Swift Testing tests; `swift test` green on Linux and macOS CI; module rules of docs/ARCHITECTURE.md respected (`scripts/check-lot-deps.py` passes).\n- [ ] Spec `docs/lots/LOT-093-*.md` with legacy sources (file:line), edge cases and intentional differences; verified protocol facts in HFR-PROTOCOL §6c under this lot's own `###`.\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
